 First, notice $f(-x)+f(x)=\arctan(-x)+\arctan \frac{1+x}{1-x}+\arctan  x + \arctan \frac{1-x}{1+x}=0 $. Therefore $f(x)$ is odd, so we only need to search the range of positive numbers $x$ Now compute
\begin{align*}
f(x) &= \arctan x + \frac{\pi}{4} - \arctan x \\
&= \frac{\pi}{4}
\end{align*}
So the range is $\boxed{\frac{\pi}{4}}$. <answer> $\frac{\pi}{4}$ </answer>

